   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.1. Increased institutional capacity of employer and business membership organizations (EBMOs)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Gambia Chamber of Commerce and Industry (GCCI) upgraded its training service on entrepreneurship and management of micro, small, and medium enterprises. To respond to an increasing demand, GCCI expanded its trainer pool by 15, focusing on ILO Tools related to business creation (Generate Your Business Idea- GYB and Start Your Business- SYB) and its new Formalize Your Business (FYB) training module. To widen its service and outreach to enterprises, GCCI appointed 12 trainers in the six administration regions of the Gambia. Notably, GCCI trained 120 entrepreneurs, among which 88 women from 19 June to 20 July 2023, and assisted them in their formalization process. 
To complement its service offer, the GCCI launched an innovative digital platform called  &#x201c;Formalize Your Business&#x201d; on 23 June 2023. The platform is a comprehensive system designed to help start-ups and enterprises formalize their operations by providing access to information, assessments of compliance with regulations, resources, and tools that will facilitate their formalization process. The platform integrates GCCI&#x2019;s formalization, business management, and entrepreneurship training offers while granting access to coaching services from GCCI&#x2019;s pool of advisors. As of 15 July 2023, 80 entrepreneurs were enrolled on the platform. 
As a result of the enhanced and integrated service offer, GCCI has been able to strengthen its outreach to newly formalized entrepreneurs and gained 155 new members especially youth-owned enterprises and business support organizations with a focus on youth and women, which were previously underrepresented in GCCI&#x2019;s membership. This includes partnerships with the African Youth Entrepreneurship Academy and Agro Incubation Hub. Moreover, GCCI established partnerships with 14 women&#x2019;s associations disseminating information on the FYB platform.
 With the contribution of the Government of Italy, the ILO provided assistance, to the training of the 15 GCCI staff and partner trainers on the GYB, SYB and FYB modules in the fourth quarter of 2022.
Using RBSA resources, the ILO supported the development of the &apos;Formalise your business&apos; training module, based on the Gambian formalization process requirements, and developed the production of the relevant training materials for trainers and learners.  The ILO also provided support to the design of the digital platform &#x2018;Formalize and Develop Your Business&#x2019; and to the development of its content based on the Gambian formalisation ecosystem and its registration and compliance procedures. Further assistance by the ILO included the training of GCCI staff to maintain and update the platform and of GCCI partner business advisors from the National Association of Business Coaches to use the platform and provide advice through it. The ILO also supported the launching of the platform, chaired by the Minister of Trade, Regional Integration and Employment and attended by 94 participants, including from UNDP, various business associations, enterprises and the media. The ILO also facilitated the implementation of an information campaign on the use of the platform. 
The ILO also provided assistance to the implementation by GCCI of a pilot initiative to assist 120 entrepreneurs in their formalization process and provide follow up by GCCI and partners advisors.</narrative>
   </description>
